{"agent":"fix-regression-tests-arg","data":{"body":"Fixes bug B227585c781. bug fixed --regression-test splits its value on ',' only, so 'a.py::t1;a.py::t2' is resolved as ONE node id and refused as 'names a test that exists in no worktree: <the whole string>' -- the input is misdiagnosed. The flag is also not repeatable: '--regression-test a --regression-test b' silently records only b. Fix: the flag appends (repeatable); each value is split on ',' and ';' outside parametrize brackets; MCP accepts the existing string and also a JSON list; every test is resolved and a refusal names only the missing ones, with a hint when one entry looks like several tests joined by whitespace. The event keeps regression_test (canonical ', '-joined string, back-compat for every reader) and adds regression_tests (the list); the fold exposes Bug.regression_tests.","globs":["ddflow/api/knowledge.py","ddflow/surfaces/cli.py","ddflow/surfaces/mcp.py","ddflow/surfaces/commands/knowledge.py","ddflow/core/model.py","tests/test_bug_fixed_regression_list.py"],"line":"","needs":[],"parent":"","priority":100,"tags":[],"title":"bug fixed accepts several regression tests: repeatable --regression-test, ';' or ',' separated, a list over MCP; a missing one is named alone (fixes bug B227585c781)"},"id":"e396f10126c2c49a3fa24c597","kind":"task.added","lamport":5691,"schema":1,"subject":"B-fix-regression-tests-arg","ts":"2026-10-01T17:38:43.140853Z"}
