{"agent":"fix-regression-tests-arg","data":{"body":"Fixes bug B227585c781. bug fixed --regression-test splits its value on ',' only, so 'a.py::t1;a.py::t2' is resolved as ONE node id and refused as 'names a test that exists in no worktree: <the whole string>' -- the input is misdiagnosed. The flag is also not repeatable: '--regression-test a --regression-test b' silently records only b. Fix: the flag appends (repeatable); each value is split on ',' and ';' outside parametrize brackets; MCP accepts the existing string and also a JSON list; every test is resolved and a refusal names only the missing ones (and how many of how many), with a hint when one entry looks like several tests joined by whitespace. The event keeps regression_test (the given string verbatim, or ', '-joined from a list -- back-compat for every reader: fold, index, bug invalid's message, CLI echo) and adds regression_tests (the split list)."},"id":"ecdac4361e9a8d3e9303f4818","kind":"task.updated","lamport":5718,"schema":1,"subject":"B-fix-regression-tests-arg","ts":"2026-10-01T17:42:38.103975Z"}
